 "standard_url": "https://nerdc.gov.ng/",
 "standard_text": "Use the laws of indices for multiplication, division and powers; use zero and negative indices; evaluate expressions with indices. (summary of the NERDC JSS 3 Mathematics curriculum)",
 "meta_desc": "Free JSS 3 maths worksheets on indices: multiplying and dividing powers, power of a power, zero and negative indices, fractional indices and evaluating. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "aᵐ × aⁿ = aᵐ⁺ⁿ, aᵐ ÷ aⁿ = aᵐ⁻ⁿ",
 "key_sub": "(aᵐ)ⁿ = aᵐⁿ, a⁰ = 1",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>When you multiply powers of the same base, add the indices: 2³ × 2⁴ = 2⁷.</li><li>When you divide, subtract the indices: 5⁶ ÷ 5² = 5⁴. A power of a power: multiply the indices.</li><li>a⁰ = 1 and a⁻ⁿ = 1 ÷ aⁿ: 3⁻² = 1/9.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>x⁵ × x³ ÷ x²</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>5 + 3 − 2</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x⁶</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>(2³)²</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>3 × 2</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 2⁶ = 64</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Multiplying the indices when multiplying powers</td><td>Add them.</td></tr><tr><td>Thinking a⁰ = 0</td><td>a⁰ = 1.</td></tr><tr><td>Making a negative index a negative number</td><td>2⁻³ = 1/8, not −8.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What is the base in 5⁴?",
   "a": "5."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is 10⁻¹?",
   "a": "0.1."
  },
  {
   "q": "Do the laws work for different bases?",
   "a": "No, only for the same base."
  }
